s","description":"Workflows that are associated with the Requested Item \\[sc\\_req\\_item\\] table have a specific type of workflow input.You can declare requested item catalog variables at the catalog item level or at a global level.You can declare global catalog variables using the Service Catalog.You can declare a catalog item-specific variable.You can declare a catalog item-specific variable directly from a catalog item record.Catalog specific item variables are visible in several places depending on where in the process the variable is viewed.The Catalog Item Variables are available and assigned to a specific Catalog Task activity \\(thereby to a specific task\\) using the slushbucket entry of a catalog task.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/c\\_WorkflowCatalogVariables.html","release":"australia","product":"Legacy Workflow","classification":"legacy-workflow","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":4,"breadcrumb":["Workflow management","Classic Workflow","ServiceNow AI Platform Additional Capabilities","Extend ServiceNow AI Platform capabilities"],"tags":["#servicenow-platform","#legacy-workflow","#classic","#deprecated","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[157,163]]},"smart_blocks:ServiceNowOfficialDocs/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/c_WorkflowCatalogVariables.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"1pdl82a","at":1784561353047},"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/c_WorkflowCatalogVariables.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,19],"size":1272,"outlinks":[],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
